+## 2026-10-05 — A bridge delivery failure and its notice are one write (#2005)
+
+<!-- prawduct: type=bugfix | scope=2005-delivery-failure-notice -->
+
+PM dispatch (Medusa 025881ed), admitted into v5.31 as one bounded pre-freeze PR.
+
+**Why.** #2005 was written against the #1799 design and says a message that failed or went `send_unknown` on the Hub is never reported back. Since #2103 the gateway does queue a failure notice for both, but as a second write after the route's own, guarded by `applied && !replayed`. A server that stopped between the two left the route already failed, so no later pass or restart ever queued the notice: the silent terminal failure the issue describes, in a narrower window.
+
+**What.**
+- `lib/bridge-gateway.js`: `_returnToMaster` and `_markUnconfirmed` return the notice as the decision's `outbound`, which `bridgeStore.applyRouteWrite` queues inside the route's transaction. The idempotency keys and the notice text are unchanged.
+- `test/bridge-gateway.test.js`: both terminal Hub states and the unknown outcome, each with the server stopping as the notice is queued; no second notice across passes, a restart or after it is posted; correlation to the operator's message; no operator words or credential in the item, the row or the audit; nothing declared while a send is still on its way.
+- `docs/operator-bridge.md`, `CHANGELOG.md`.
+
+**Not in it.** `_launchFailed` still queues its notice by a separate write. A failed launch is not a Hub delivery state, so it is outside the dispatch; flagged to the PM.
+
+**Root cause.** The route write and the notice were made atomic nowhere, although the store already offered it; five of the eight new tests pass on the old code, which is how narrow the window was.
+
+**Classification:** bugfix
+
